        "Content": "Waterfront living opposite Sheen Falls\r\n\r\nPanoramic Kenmare Bay views | Turnkey B3\r\nRated home | c.132 sq m gross / c.1,400 sq ft gross| 3 double bedrooms | Walk to Kenmare\r\n \r\nA Rare Kenmare Combination\r\nOccupying an exceptional waterside setting overlooking Kenmare Bay and directly opposite the renowned Sheen Falls Estate, this extensively renovated three-bedroom home combines panoramic water and mountain views, refined contemporary interiors and the rare convenience of being within an easy walk of Kenmare town.\r\n\r\nExtensively upgraded in 2025 and now achieving a B3 BER, this 132 sqm/1400 sq ft semi-detached residence has been designed around its remarkable setting. Water and mountain views are enjoyed throughout the house - from the open-plan kitchen, dining and living space to the principal and guest bedrooms - while a south-facing landscaped garden and expansive terrace create an exceptional outdoor living space overlooking the bay.\r\nThe combination is difficult to replicate in Kenmare: panoramic views, turnkey condition, excellent energy performance and low-maintenance living, approximately 1.3km from the town centre, restaurants, shops, services and golf club via illuminated footpaths.\r\n\r\nThe Residence\r\nThe residence has undergone a comprehensive programme of upgrades and modernisation focused on energy efficiency, durability and refined contemporary living. Significant investment has been made in high-performance glazing, insulation, heating systems, kitchen and utility spaces, bathrooms, interior finishes and landscaping. The result is a highly efficient, low-maintenance home that can be occupied immediately.\r\nNatural light and the panoramic setting inform the house throughout. The principal rooms have been arranged and finished to maximise the relationship with the bay, mountains and woodland beyond, while the elevated terraces extend the living space outdoors.\r\n\r\nGround Floor\r\nEntrance Hall & Guest WC\r\nA bright entrance hall with wood-effect laminate flooring, under-stairs storage and smart electric radiator leads to the principal ground-floor accommodation. The guest WC is fitted with contemporary wall-hung storage, LED mirror and smart electric towel rail.\r\n\r\nOpen-Plan Kitchen, Dining & Living\r\nA spacious, bright triple-aspect room with water views from every window forms the heart of the house. Wood-effect laminate flooring runs throughout, with an 8kW wood-burning stove anchoring the living area and French doors opening onto the terrace overlooking Kenmare Bay.\r\nThe contemporary Nolte kitchen features pale oak cabinetry, a generous island with induction hob and integrated extractor, Cosentino stone worktops, Neff stainless-steel double ovens, integrated full-height larder fridge and dishwasher, and a Quooker tap providing instant boiling and filtered water.\r\n\r\nUtility Room\r\nDesigned to maximise storage and functionality, the utility includes a stainless-steel sink with pull-out spray tap, integrated full-height Neff larder freezer and provision for recessed washing machine and heat-pump dryer. The room also enjoys a water view.\r\n\r\nFirst Floor\r\n\r\nPrincipal Bedroom & Ensuite\r\nA bright dual-aspect double bedroom with water views, custom blinds and smart electric heating. The tiled ensuite includes a high-pressure shower, wall-hung vanity storage, mirrored storage and smart electric towel rail.\r\n\r\nBedroom Two\r\nA generous guest double bedroom with a large window framing striking water and mountain views, custom blind and smart electric heating.\r\n\r\nBedroom Three\r\nA further double bedroom, currently used as a dressing room, with views across the rear garden towards the water and mountains.\r\n\r\nMain Bathroom\r\nFinished with Porcelanosa floor and wall tiles, the main bathroom includes a freestanding slipper bath with floor-mounted filler, separate large walk-in high-pressure shower, wall-hung vanity, mirrored storage and smart electric towel rail.\r\n\r\nStorage\r\nThe upper hallway includes substantial custom recessed linen storage. A pull-down stair provides access to a spacious, floored, reinsulated and illuminated attic, ideal for additional storage.\r\n\r\nGardens, Terrace & Setting\r\nThe property enjoys a southerly aspect, with the rear garden receiving excellent sunlight throughout the day. Professionally designed for easy maintenance, the gardens combine raised beds, gravelled areas and colourful perennial planting, herbs and shrubs.\r\n\r\nThe expansive elevated terrace, finished in composite decking, is a defining feature: an outdoor room for dining and entertaining with panoramic views over the Kenmare Bay estuary towards the Caha and Sheehy Mountains, woodland and the protected grounds of the five-star Sheen Falls Estate.\r\nA powered 3m x 2m Steeltech garden building provides useful storage or hobby space. Private off-road parking is available for up to four cars. Shared landscaped gardens and foreshore seating areas form part of the development amenities.\r\n\r\nRenovation & Energy Performance\r\nComprehensive renovation and modernisation completed in 2025\r\nBER improved from D1 to B3\r\nTriple-glazed Rationel windows and doors\r\nInsulation upgrades\r\nSmart app-controlled thermostatic electric heating throughout\r\nHigh-capacity hot-water cylinder with additional pump, pressure and digital controls\r\nContemporary German Nolte kitchen with premium integrated appliances\r\nPorcelanosa bathroom finishes\r\nProfessionally landscaped low-maintenance gardens\r\n\r\nLocation\r\n18 Inbhear Scéine occupies a particularly attractive position in Killowen, overlooking Kenmare Bay and directly opposite the renowned Sheen Falls Estate. Kenmare town centre is approximately 1.3km away via illuminated footpaths, placing restaurants, cafés, independent shops, supermarkets, services and Kenmare Golf Club within easy walking distance.\r\n\r\nThe combination of panoramic water and mountain views with genuine walkability is unusual in the Kenmare market. The property is well suited to permanent occupation, an easily managed second home or a lock-up-and-leave base for enjoying the Ring of Kerry and Beara Peninsula.\r\nThe property's established planning status permits both full-time residential and holiday-home use.\r\n\r\nKey Facts\r\nc.130 sq m / c.1,400 sq ft\r\nThree double bedrooms\r\nPrincipal ensuite, main bathroom and ground-floor guest WC\r\nTriple-aspect open-plan kitchen/dining/living room\r\nSouth-facing landscaped garden\r\nElevated composite terrace with panoramic views\r\nPowered Steeltech garden building\r\nPrivate parking for up to four cars\r\nHigh-speed fibre broadband\r\nB3 BER\r\nTurnkey condition\r\n\r\nServices & Management\r\nMains water\r\nMains sewerage\r\nMains electricity\r\nHigh-speed fibre broadband & SKY TV installed \r\nSmart app-controlled electric heating system\r\nRing Video doorbell\r\n\r\nPrivate estate community fee: \r\n€70 per month, covering sewerage, waste/recycling, public lighting, communal grounds maintenance and public liability insurance.\r\nShared landscaped gardens and foreshore seating areas are included as part of the development amenities.\r\n\r\nViewing\r\nThe setting and outlook are central to the appeal of 18 Inbhear Scéine and are best appreciated in person. \r\nViewing is recommended by appointment with the selling agent."
      },
